ZVSE2

** FORGE & FURY - DEPENDENCY CHECK
**
** Forge & Fury is an add-on for several mods. Every feature that needs another mod checks one of
** these flags and switches itself off when that mod is not enabled, so the rest still works:
**
**   i^cr_hasResound^    ResOunD (Emerald artifacts, Third Upgrade Mod creatures)
**   i^cr_hasACM^        Advanced Classes Mod
**   i^cr_hasHenchmen^   Enhanced Henchmen
**   i^cr_hasEraScripts^ ERA Scripts (option 996, replaced by Attack Speed)
**   i^cr_hasEasyCheats^ Easy Cheats
**
** A mod counts as enabled when one of its script files is visible in the game's virtual file
** system (only enabled mods are mapped there). The "31" prefix makes this script load before
** all other Forge & Fury scripts.

!?FU(CR_CheckDependencies);
!!FU(FileExists):P^Data/s/Third Upgrade Mod.erm^/?i^cr_hasResound^;
!!FU(FileExists):P^Data/s/advanced classes skills.erm^/?i^cr_hasACM^;
!!FU(FileExists):P^Data/s/1000 wog - henchmen consts.erm^/?i^cr_hasHenchmen^;
!!FU(FileExists):P^Data/s/option 996 - gnolls-marauders strike first.erm^/?i^cr_hasEraScripts^;
!!FU(FileExists):P^Data/s/easy cheats.erm^/?i^cr_hasEasyCheats^;

!#FU(CR_CheckDependencies):P;

; Named globals are stored in savegames: check again after a game is started or loaded
; (this handler runs before the OnStartOrLoad handlers of the other Forge & Fury scripts).
!?FU(OnStartOrLoad);
!!FU(CR_CheckDependencies):P;
